cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this companion software, please cite the archived software release and the corresponding Springer book."
title: "Companion Computational Codes for Computational Metal Additive Manufacturing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Hosseinzadeh"
    given-names: "Hamed"
version: "0.1.0-dev"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Educational source-code implementations accompanying the Springer book
  Computational Metal Additive Manufacturing: Advanced Multiphysics and
  AI-Enhanced Simulation. The repository includes selected examples in
  multiphysics simulation, non-fusion metal AM, AI/PINNs, DfAM, fatigue,
  reduced-order modeling, and digital-twin workflows.
